---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { CardGrid, LinkCard } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
const repo = 'https://github.com/0x101/agent-harness-101';
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Agent Harness 101',
    template: 'splash',
    hero: {
      tagline:
        'Learn agent harness engineering by growing a deliberately naive coding agent, one measured change at a time.',
      actions: [
        { text: 'Start with the curriculum', link: '/curriculum/', variant: 'primary' },
        { text: 'Browse the readings', link: '/readings/', variant: 'minimal' },
      ],
    },
  }}
>
  <p>
    Agent Harness 101 is a 42-session course. You start with an agent of about a hundred lines: one bash
    tool, no output truncation, no memory management, and no check on its own work. Over ten modules
    you add the components real harnesses have, in the order the literature motivates them: tool
    output truncation, file and edit tools, stuck detection, context management, planning, subagents,
    verification gates, and finally an outer loop that proposes changes to the harness itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every change is measured against a twelve-task eval set, with pass rate and token counts side by
    side, so you learn what each component is worth rather than taking it on faith. Each session pairs
    the build with the paper or post that motivates it.
  </p>

  <h2>Three ways in</h2>
  <CardGrid>
    <LinkCard
      title="Read the site"
      description="The curriculum session by session, with a guide for each reading and links to the sources. No setup."
      href="/curriculum/"
    />
    <LinkCard
      title="Run the lab"
      description="Create your own repository from the template, open it in Claude Code, and type /today. Your agent, your logs, your numbers."
      href="/lab/"
    />
    <LinkCard
      title="Open in Codespaces"
      description="The same lab with no local setup. The devcontainer installs the dependencies and forwards the lab server."
      href={repo}
    />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>What is in the box</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/curriculum/">Curriculum</a>: 42 sessions across 10 modules, each with a read, a build and a measure step.</li>
    <li><a href="/readings/">Readings</a>: 22 papers, 12 posts and 2 repositories, each with a guide to what to read and what to skip.</li>
    <li><a href="/lab/">Lab</a>: the eval runner, the twelve tasks, the naive agent, and the tutor that runs each session with you.</li>
    <li><a href={repo}>Source</a>: the code is MIT licensed and the course text is CC BY 4.0.</li>
  </ul>
</StarlightPage>
